    "result_text": "Green. Both findings addressed.\n\n## What I did\n\nBoth findings were correct \u2014 my original change silently invalidated the justification for the `OwnerCity` extraction without cleaning up around it. I agreed with both and fixed them together:\n\n- **Finding 1 (orphaned `OwnerCity`)**: With `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` no longer using it, `countOwnersInCity` had a single caller, so the \"shared by two, extracted to stay consistent\" rationale was dead. Rather than just patch the misleading javadoc, I inlined the count back into `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` and deleted `OwnerCity.java` \u2014 the extraction no longer earns its keep.\n\n- **Finding 2 (stale `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` javadoc)**: Removed the *\"consistent with `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`'s per-city sequence\"* clause, which pointed at logic that no longer exists. Kept the factual \"city is matched exactly\" note.\n\nVerified no references to the deleted `OwnerCity` remain (the lingering `OwnerCityAtCapacity*` matches are the unrelated capacity exception/handler), and the acceptance suite still passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
